WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.310
<i>I'm Hasegawa Kouta, a 17-year-old second-year
high school student who likes Sanrio.</i>

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>Yuu and Yoshino are the first friends
I've made because of Sanrio.</i>

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.870
<i>However...</i>

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.090
<i>The other day Yuu had a big fight
with his little sister, Yuri-chan,</i>

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.170
<i>but they seem to have 
made up, which is a relief.</i>

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.510
<i>And this time, there's something
going on with Yoshino...</i>

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:30.810
Yoshino?

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.170
Uh-oh...

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.850
Hey, Yoshino! What happened
in yesterday's game?

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.810
That was my bad. I'll do better next time.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.980
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.650
All right, that's enough!

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.070
Matsuo...

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.230
Nice timing, Tomo-san.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.180
Huh?

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.470
Matsuo Tomo-san,
he's the soccer team captain.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:05.410
He would look after us when
we were on the soccer team as kids.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.250
The hell? You're way too forgiving as captain.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.720
Okay, I'll hear your complaints over there!

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.460
Hey!

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.260
Let go!

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.260
Shun.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.260
You need to take a hint, too.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.370
Now then, summer isn't going to wait forever!

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.730
You don't need to tell us that... besides, I was...

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.240
What does he mean by take a hint?

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.690
I don't get it.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.430
Yoshino.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.200
You guys...

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.260
Oh, yeah. You guys lost yesterday's
practice match, didn't you?

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.890
Huh? And they're blaming it on you?

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.930
I thought soccer was a team sport?

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:49.790
It's not fair just to blame you.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.250
That's none of your business.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.760
I won't lose next time.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.760
Because you have the goddess of victory?

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.560
Huh?

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.440
Oh, that's right, you always have that thing...

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.230
<b>Factoid: There are charms for 21 different Sanrio characters.</b>

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:06.760
Yeah.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.890
Kitty-san is

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.700
my goddess of victory.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.740
Hello Friends!

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.250
So awesome!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.760
Sorry, I fumbled that pass,

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.500
but I'll do better next time.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.030
Don't worry about it, I'll clinch it for us.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:08.890
Wha?

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.970
Yoshino, we're going to confirm the play.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.540
I'll figure it out.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.810
H-Hey!

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.000
What a pain.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.370
Yoshino-kun is so awesome today!

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.860
He's totally cool!

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.910
<i>I wouldn't say "cool"...</i>

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.540
<i>it's... more like he's the one</i>

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.390
<i>who can't be a team player...</i>

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:44.930
Hey, Yoshi—

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.930
What the heck is his deal?

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.870
We're trying for nationals this year.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.570
Does he think he's going to win on his own?

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.960
He just doesn't get it.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.850
Um... here!

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.590
I'm rooting for you.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.010
<i>I'm rooting for you.</i>

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.000
What a pain.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.480
<i>Hey, Yuu... Why is Yoshino like that?</i>

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.980
Hmm? What do you mean?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:49.370
He doesn't try to get along with his soccer
teammates and he's cold to his female fans.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.510
Oh, that.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.450
<i>You've been friends since you were kids, right?</i>

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.700
So then, why is he—

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:56.450
<i>Kouta,</i>

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.330
are you really worried about him?

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.750
Of course I am!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.530
I mean,

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.730
I'm his friend.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.930
Shunsuke is...

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:13.930
like a cat.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.560
You know, his personality?

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:28.790
He's always saying how caring
for people and things like that are a pain.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.920
It's okay for you to worry about him,

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.250
but if you meddle too much,
you might get scratched.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.420
<i>Because he's a cat?</i>

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.220
Yep.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.850
<i>Oh, that's right. That Hello Kitty charm...</i>

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.960
<i>I guess that's a cat, too.</i>

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.670
Now that I think about it, that was probably
the catalyst for him liking Hello Kitty.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.480
I'm rooting for you.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.990
We'll definitely win the next game!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.500
I'll show you my medal!

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.370
All right!

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:26.700
You did it!

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.390
You did it, Shushu!

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.630
Yeah!

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.180
We won that time because
I had Kitty-san with me.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.180
We'll win next time.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.950
So Yoshino actually accepted presents before?

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.470
You're talking about yesterday?

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:00.330
I guess he must've really liked that girl then.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.460
No idea.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:06.170
I mean, that girl moved right after that.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.420
Really?!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.340
He must've gotten over it a long time ago.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.820
He also changes his Hello
Kitty charm every year.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.180
I see...

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:20.530
Anyway, with that charm he managed
to escape from a serious losing streak.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.190
Ever since then, Hello Kitty has
been Shushu's goddess of victory.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.270
Speaking of, where is Yoshino?

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.610
He's with Tomo-san. They had
something to talk about apparently.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.460
I see,

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:39.090
so that's what you've decided?

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.410
Yeah.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.980
If I can carry the game
there'll be no problems.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.650
We'll definitely win then.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:48.790
<i>So long as I have Kitty-san.</i>

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.460
You still don't get it, do you?

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.520
Huh?

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.970
I know this is sudden,

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.970
but I've removed Yoshino from the starters.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:06.020
For now I'm going to have him
serve as support for the team.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.480
That's the plan, everyone.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.580
He's removing... <i>me</i>?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.340
Let's go!

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.190
What the heck is going on?

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.200
Why am I being removed?

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.250
<i>I was definitely going to win the next time...</i>

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.660
<i>I was going to make the team win.</i>

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:30.460
Yoshino!

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.920
Make sure you're paying
attention to what we're doing!

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:40.740
<i>So I'm just supposed to sit here twiddling
my thumbs and watch others play?</i>

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.660
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.470
The hell...

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:54.630
What the hell?!

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:03.610
Damn it!

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.460
Seriously, I'm not joking.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.670
Seriously!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.120
You're not joking?

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:12.690
Move it.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:21.180
Yoshino-kun's been pretty agitated lately.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.560
Well, you know what happened
with the soccer team...

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.380
<i>Dang it, every single person!</i>

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.030
Sorry...

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.510
Huh?

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:00.900
There used to be all kinds of screaming
at the morning practices until just recently.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.300
Yuu...

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.390
You're the only one who came,
even though all the girls aren't here.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:12.280
Perhaps we should dress
you up as a girl instead?

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:13.810
Not here...

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.300
That's what I mean, you should
scream for the girls that aren't—

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:18.700
Yoshino's not here.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:19.920
Huh?

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:23.280
He came to school, didn't he? Right?

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.280
Hey,

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.470
was Shun absent today?

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.810
Have you heard anything?

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.400
It's to be expected, isn't it?

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:36.660
You of all people should know
how seriously Shunsuke takes soccer

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:40.900
and how much he wants to win, Tomo-san.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.310
So—

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.480
That's why.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:44.280
Huh?

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:47.640
Will you listen to what I have to say?

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.380
Me, too?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.750
You guys are Shun's friends after all.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.670
I don't get it.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:04.950
What the heck?

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.000
I...

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.440
<i>I...</i>

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.180
<i>I've been taken off the team.</i>

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:27.410
<i>I can't play in the games.</i>

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:34.900
<i>And...</i>

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.200
And just how the hell are we going to win?!

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:12.930
Some... Some...

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.700
Some goddess of victory you are!

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:18.520
Yoshino!

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.250
You...

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:28.990
Don't do it.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:32.470
Anything but that!

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.550
Tomo-san asked us to help.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.330
Let's play some soccer!

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.400
Sorry about that.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:08.070
Here I go!

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.730
You idiot...

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:18.720
Keep your eye on the ball!

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.410
That happens because you're not—

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:25.160
Make sure you're paying
attention to what we're doing!

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:31.670
I wasn't paying attention,
so I couldn't see properly?

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.880
Tomo-san is amazing as ever.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.600
He's always thinking about you and the team.

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:45.360
You know, depending on how the
summer ends, the third-years are retiring.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.580
We only made it into the best 16,

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.980
but apparently everyone is
aiming much higher this year.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.490
That's because...

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:58.810
you're there.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:03.180
That's why the seniors are
so worked up about this.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:05.590
You'll accept

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:08.480
their feelings, right?

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.190
It's a pain in the ass.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.290
Come on now.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:20.830
Tomo-san said he compromised
with the team for you, and...

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:21.700
Hey.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.190
Why are you running away?

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:27.140
Oh, sorry!

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:30.900
It's just that after watching
you this whole time, that's how I felt.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.120
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.050
I just don't like annoying—

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:37.650
Kouta's right.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:42.440
You've been running away.
Ever since that day.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:47.540
I-I...

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:51.800
Just...

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:10.150
She never said anything and just disappeared.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.510
Ever since then, I've been
afraid to face other people.

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:19.390
What's the point of even being friends with
anyone when they're just going to disappear?

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:20.700
And...

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.950
Kitty-san was the only one who stayed.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:33.940
Yoshino...

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:39.550
I didn't get it when I was
removed from the starters.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.090
My teammates are just
going to disappear anyway

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:47.890
and we're going to have to go
our separate ways someday.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:52.590
When I thought about that... it scared me.

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.060
Kitty-san will always be there for me.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:59.360
It was like I was praying
to some divine power

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.340
and then I could avoid all my scared feelings.

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:05.590
Kitty-san will help me win.

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:09.420
With Kitty-san by my side,
everything would work out.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.130
And when everything didn't work out,

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.620
I blamed her and tried to throw her away!

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:24.970
That's right. I've always been running away.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.910
I... I'm...

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.030
A kind person.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:33.790
I always thought you were kind of scary,

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.760
but I was totally wrong.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:41.240
You're incredibly kind and because
of that, you try to avoid hurting others.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:45.410
No, I'm just a coward trying to
keep himself from getting hurt.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:49.140
But it's because you care
so much that you get hurt, right?

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:52.450
You care, so you don't want them to hate you.

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:54.630
So instead, you're unable
to get close to anyone, right?

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.640
I'm sorry, Shunsuke.

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:00.850
Yuu...

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:04.910
I always thought that you were so strong.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:08.110
But I was the closest one to you
and I didn't even notice.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.560
Yeah! You've been
facing Yuu this whole time!

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:15.690
You can totally face other people, then!

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.700
No, even with Yuu I'm...

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.280
Come on! Come here!

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.450
I'm ready,

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.960
you can approach me!

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:29.960
No...

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:36.210
Come on.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:38.650
You guys...

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:40.690
Come here!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.700
What the heck...

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:55.460
I don't get it.

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:13.990
The more panicked we get,
the harder it is for him.

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.440
<i>It's still not time yet,</i>

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:24.670
<i>for Yoshino's sake and the
sake of the whole team.</i>

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.410
Please look after me!

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:51.190
What're you staring at?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.920
Whaddya mean what're we staring at?!

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.140
What's with you all the sudden?!

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:59.630
That came out of nowhere!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.800
Besides, you're supposed
to say that when you come in!

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:16.690
So you're back to being one of the starters?

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.910
Pretty much.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.460
I'm really glad!

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.610
Huh? Where's my thank you?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.700
Why would I say that now?

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:28.410
Never mind me, what about Kouta's?

00:20:28.650 --> 00:20:29.450
Huh?

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.440
Thanks, Kouta.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:45.640
Hey, did you just say my name?
Did you call me Kouta?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.480
Er, I was just following suit with Yuu...

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.550
Then I'm going to call you Shunsuke, okay?

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:52.930
Listen to what people are saying, would ya?

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.020
Did you hear that, Yuu? He called me Kouta!

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:02.710
Hey, Tsucchi, I've realized something.

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:06.440
I haven't exchanged a single 
word with Hase today either.

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:10.020
I was thinking about asking him
to hang out but he just disappeared.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.100
I wonder if he got a girlfriend or something?

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:15.250
But normally he would've told us
if he'd gotten a girlfriend, right?

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.170
We're his best friends, right?

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:20.700
I'm so lonely, so lonely, Hase!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.430
Hey, where's Hase by the way?

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:23.230
Huh?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:27.030
Were you listening to what
I was saying at all?

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:07.760
You should be ashamed!

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:10.660
What's all the noise?

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.160
You freak!

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:20.120
So that means you're
asking for a fight then, right?

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:23.210
Wait!

